# Purpose

Interaction defines how Aura responds to every user action.

Every touch, animation, transition and response should make the interface feel alive, predictable and effortless.

Interactions are never decorative.

They communicate intent, feedback and state.

---

# Philosophy

Aura should feel less like software...

and more like touching physical objects.

The interface should feel responsive before users consciously notice it.

Nothing should ever feel delayed.

Nothing should ever surprise the user.

---

# Core Principles

Immediate

Responsive

Predictable

Elegant

Calm

Forgiving

Consistent

---

# Touch Response

Every touch receives immediate visual feedback.

Target response time:

< 50 milliseconds

Touch feedback should begin before the action is completed.

---

# Tap

Tap is the primary interaction.

Expected behavior

Touch

↓

Immediate visual compression

↓

Optional haptic

↓

Action

↓

State update

↓

Return to idle

---

# Button Behavior

Buttons should compress naturally.

Scale

100%

↓

97%

↓

100%

Animation

Spring

Duration

0.18s

No button should ever "flash."

---

# Card Interaction

Cards are interactive surfaces.

Touch

↓

Subtle elevation change

↓

Small scale reduction

↓

Optional glow

↓

Navigation or action

Cards should feel soft.

Never rigid.

---

# Long Press

Purpose

Reveal advanced functionality.

Examples

Rename

Move

Favorite

Diagnostics

Long press must never contain essential actions.

---

# Swipe

Allowed

Delete

Favorite

Archive

Mute

Pin

Not Allowed

Open Settings

Run Scenes

Critical actions

---

# Scroll Behavior

Scrolling should feel natural.

Momentum should match native iOS.

Never interfere with system gestures.

---

# Pull to Refresh

Refresh begins immediately.

Progress indicator appears naturally.

Never block scrolling.

---

# Loading Behavior

Aura avoids waiting whenever possible.

Preferred order

Cached Content

↓

Skeleton

↓

Live Content

↓

Animated Update

Avoid blank screens.

---

# State Transitions

State changes should animate.

Offline

↓

Connecting

↓

Online

Not

Offline

↓

Instantly Online

Transitions explain what changed.

---

# Device Status

Online

Small fade.

Offline

Soft desaturation.

Busy

Gentle pulse.

Updating

Progress animation.

Error

Subtle shake once.

---

# Scene Execution

Example

Movie Night

User taps

↓

Medium haptic

↓

Hero card expands

↓

Progress indicator

↓

Lights respond

↓

