---

# Accessibility

Every interaction must support

Reduce Motion

VoiceOver

Switch Control

Dynamic Type

Assistive Touch

When Reduce Motion is enabled

Replace movement with opacity transitions.

---

# One-Handed Usage

Primary actions should remain reachable.

Avoid placing important controls in the extreme top-right corner.

Frequently used controls belong near the lower third of the screen.

---

# Interruptions

Incoming events should never reset user progress.

Examples

Network reconnect

Background refresh

Device status changes

All updates should preserve the current interaction.

---

# Delight Moments

Aura may occasionally reward the user with subtle moments.

Examples

Scene completed.

New device added.

Automation created.

These moments should feel satisfying without becoming playful.

---

# Anti-Patterns

Never use

Blocking loading screens

Unexpected navigation

Multiple confirmation dialogs

Flashing elements

Oversized animations

Auto-playing tutorials

Forced onboarding

Aggressive notifications

---

# Interaction Checklist

Before approving any interaction ask:

Does it feel immediate?

Does it feel native?

Can it be completed with fewer steps?

Is feedback clear?

Would this still feel premium after years of use?

If any answer is "No"

Redesign the interaction.

---

# Golden Rule

Every interaction should leave the interface feeling calmer than before it was touched.

